From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 20:04:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] selftests: apple-dcp: define DATA_CONNECTION in the
 lifecycle tipd mock

c1398b6a40 ("usb: typec: tipd: keep the USB host when a partner only
completes PD") adds CD321X_ROUTE_BITS to drivers/usb/typec/tipd/cd321x-dp.h,
and that mask names TPS_DATA_STATUS_DATA_CONNECTION. The lifecycle harness
pastes cd321x-dp.h (without its includes) into its test unit next to its own
mock of the tps6598x.h DATA_STATUS bits, which had no DATA_CONNECTION. Three
units (physical-disconnect, fast-replug-bounce, dropped-swap-teardown)
stopped compiling.

Define it at bit 10, which no other mock DATA_STATUS bit uses (the mock
layout is its own: HPD_LEVEL is bit 8, HPD_IRQ bit 9). The harness never
calls cd321x_partner_completed(), the only user of the mask, and its own
cd321x_typec_update_mode() replaces the one in core.c that tests
DATA_CONNECTION, so no fixture result depends on the value. The
cd321x-dp KUnit cases cover the route mask.

[j604: harness-only fixup for the c1398b6a40 pick; run.py
87 ok (1 SKIP j616s) / 0 not ok on 4716ab495e with it, 84 / 3 without]
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5.5
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 tools/testing/selftests/drivers/gpu/apple-dcp/lifecycle.py | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/tools/testing/selftests/drivers/gpu/apple-dcp/lifecycle.py b/tools/testing/selftests/drivers/gpu/apple-dcp/lifecycle.py
index 203114198f..0f9ac76ffd 100644
--- a/tools/testing/selftests/drivers/gpu/apple-dcp/lifecycle.py
+++ b/tools/testing/selftests/drivers/gpu/apple-dcp/lifecycle.py
@@ -99,6 +99,7 @@ typedef uint32_t u32; typedef uint64_t u64;
 #define TPS_DATA_STATUS_USB_DATA_ROLE (1U << 6)
 #define CD321X_DATA_STATUS_USB4_CONNECTION (1U << 7)
 #define CD321X_DATA_STATUS_HPD_LEVEL (1U << 8)
+#define TPS_DATA_STATUS_DATA_CONNECTION (1U << 10)
 #define TPS_POWER_STATUS_PWROPMODE(x) (x)
 #define TPS_STATUS_TO_UPSIDE_DOWN(x) ((x)&TPS_STATUS_PLUG_UPSIDE_DOWN)
 #define TPS_STATUS_TO_TYPEC_PORTROLE(x) 0
